 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Removing the condition at infinity",
 "statement": "Let $C_0$ be a nonempty open of $\\mathbf P^1_{k_0}$ and $F_0$ a lisse\nWeil sheaf on $C_0$, punctually $\\iota$-pure of weight $w$. Then for every\n$r\\in\\mathbf Z$, $H_c^r(C,F)$ has weights at most $w+r$, without a\nramification restriction at the original infinity.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/main-20261015/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-l-dl-general-open-line/_section.md",
  "place": "node sk-l-dl-general-open-line, order 3171"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "sk-d-dl-a1-setup",
  "sk-d-dl-general-weights"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "After a finite constant extension, choose a rational point of $C_0$\nand send it to $\\infty$ by an automorphism of $\\mathbf P^1$.\nWrite $j:C\\hookrightarrow\\mathbf P^1$, $J=j_*F$ and\n$H=J|_{\\mathbf A^1}$. This is the ordinary middle extension from\n$C\\setminus\\{\\infty\\}$, and its lisse sheaf is unramified at the new\ninfinity. Thus [sk-thm-dl-a1-upper] applies. Localization gives\n\n$$\nH_c^1(\\mathbf A^1,H)\\twoheadrightarrow H^1(\\mathbf P^1,J),\n\\qquad H_c^2(\\mathbf A^1,H)\\simeq H^2(\\mathbf P^1,J).\n$$",
   "uses": [
    "sk-thm-dl-a1-upper"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  },
  {
   "text": "Also $H^0(\\mathbf P^1,J)=H^0(C,F)$ injects into $F_{\\bar\\infty}$,\nso has weight $w$. The finite-support quotient $B=J/j_!F$ has weights\nat most $w$ by [sk-p-real-semi]. The exact sequence\n$0\\to j_!F\\to J\\to B\\to0$ now gives the desired bounds: in degree\none use $H^0(B)\\to H_c^1(C,F)\\to H^1(\\mathbf P^1,J)\\to0$;\ndegrees zero and two follow by injection and isomorphism, respectively.\nThe other degrees vanish. Constant extension replaces Frobenius by a\npower and preserves normalized weights, so the bounds descend.",
   "uses": [],
   "elementary": null
  }
 ],
 "proof_deps": [
  "sk-thm-dl-a1-upper"
 ],
